# {{ name }}

Django REST API generated by [django-api-starter](https://pypi.org/project/django-api-starter/).

Included: an email-based custom user, JWT authentication (access and refresh tokens with rotation and blacklisting), profile and password APIs{% if two_factor %}, email OTP verification and optional two-factor login{% endif %}, and admin-only user management.

## Getting started

{% if docker %}
### With Docker

```bash
docker compose up --build
docker compose exec web python manage.py createsuperuser
```

### Without Docker

{% endif %}
```bash
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate        # Windows: .venv\Scripts\activate
pip install -r requirements/development.txt
{% if database == "postgres" %}
# Set DATABASE_URL in .env to your PostgreSQL server first.
{% endif %}
python manage.py migrate
python manage.py createsuperuser
python manage.py runserver
```

The generator created `.env` with a random `SECRET_KEY`. `.env.example` documents every setting.

In development, emails (such as {% if two_factor %}OTP codes and {% endif %}password reset links) are printed to the console.

